Wings patch 0001: read the encryption key from ODYSSEUS_APP_KEY

Upstream keeps its Fernet keys (data/.app_key for database secrets, data/.key
for api_keys.json and webhook secrets) inside the data directory, so every
copy of the data volume, including backups, carries the key that decrypts it.
With this patch both key users take the key from ODYSSEUS_APP_KEY (or from
wings.keyholder, where the Wings launcher moves it so child processes do not
inherit it) and never write a key file in that mode. A malformed key, or an
existing key file that differs from the variable, raises instead of silently
generating a new key and orphaning stored secrets; with WINGS_KEY_FROM_ENV=1 a
process that lacks the key refuses to create a key file at all.
scripts/generate_env_reference.py and website/configuration-reference.md
document the variable (upstream's test fails on any undocumented variable).

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

